<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62953" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ληπ-τός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαμβάνω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be apprehended</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγῳ καὶ διανοίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					529d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ λογισμῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Max.Tyr.
					7.5
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς αἴσθησιν</span> Chryserm.
			ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				8.741
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> later, <i>to
				be apprehended by the senses</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοητός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.354.6
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Stoic
			philos., <i>acceptable</i>, not to be refused if offered, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				3.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίληπτος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				896b6
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
